version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-09"
abstract: >
  LOKI is a research prototype and open-source desktop automation system
  for macOS that uses native accessibility trees as the primary observation
  layer and locally-running large language models for multi-agent
  orchestration. Users describe tasks in natural language, and LOKI plans
  and executes them across browsers and native applications. Developed as
  a Final Year Project at Sunway University.
